## Firewall and forward-resolution split

For each scored specimen, exclude that complete specimen from outcome fitting, state reconstruction, expected-curve construction, templates, registration, residualization, basis/FPCA/PLS, scaling, tuning, and calibration.

A capacity donor is eligible only when its t+3 target date is strictly earlier than the scored t date; resistance requires t+2 strictly earlier. Same-day resolution is excluded. Inner validation repeats held-specimen/latest-target masks and refits all preprocessing.

At q30, operational inputs are RPT0 values, history through t-1, and current samples through q30. At q44/V360 they may additionally use samples through that clock. Current completed capacity/resistance, achieved current/future exposure, current summary fields without within-RPT availability time, completed span/end voltage, post-clock rows, and future records are forbidden. Measured `C[t]`/`R[t]` enter only labeled retrospective models.

Poisoning rows after q30, q44, and V360 must respectively leave each clock's operational features/predictions unchanged; poisoning current/future summaries must not change V360 operational results. Feature ancestry records source member, column, row, and latest sample.

## Separating support, warp, and amplitude

The raw segment is `V(q),t(q),I(q),T(q)` after q30.

**Fixed core versus extension.** The confirmatory morphology support is the identical physical interval `q/C0 in [0.30,0.44]`, represented at 57 equally spaced points and observed before V360 for every primary row. q44-to-V360 is a variable extension. Its duration, charge, endpoint q/C0, voltage landmarks, and masks are scientifically meaningful warp/acquisition information, but gain confined there cannot establish morphology independent of observation length. Score q44 and V360 on the same 200/166 origins.

**Coordinates.** Analyze identical raw core samples under:

- operational physical charge `x0=q/C0`;
- generated-current-capacity `xG=q/C_hat[t]`, where C_hat is strictly out-of-specimen/forward-date cross-fitted at the clock;
- retrospective measured-current-capacity `xT=q/C[t]`.

Coordinates never alter raw rows. The audit found q30 spans 0.30–0.5456 and q44 0.44–0.8002 as fractions of measured current capacity. `C/2 Capacity` and bivariate current state are retrospective sensitivities, not independent truth.

Represent rate/time warp by monotone `t(q)`, signed-current deviations, and integration discrepancy. Because time and charge are nearly collinear, retain both for prediction/diagnosis but regularize them as one acquisition block and prohibit unstable coefficient interpretation.

**Training-only registration.** Within each outer/inner training partition and family, estimate an expected fixed-core curve from strictly earlier other-specimen increments conditional on nominal temperature, cubic stage, prior capacity slope, and resolved history. Register each core with monotone cubic warp gamma anchored at endpoints, derivative bounded [0.5,2], and second-difference penalty selected only in inner folds. Registration sees curves/templates but no current/future outcome.

Keep separate:

- phase/warp: `gamma(x)-x`, voltage-landmark positions, `t(q)`, `I(q)`, extension length;
- registered amplitude: `a(x)=V(gamma^{-1}(x))-V_expected(x)`;
- unregistered residual as sensitivity.

This is operational, not unique physical phase/amplitude truth. Repeat in x0/xG/xT and with derivative bounds [0.67,1.5]. Coordinate/penalty sign reversal is inconclusive.

## Matched simple and functional alternatives

All models share rows, clocks, nuisances, family weights, targets, and nested tuning.

**Structured ridge baseline.** Common nuisance block: resolved history, q30 representation, family, nominal temperature, cubic stage/family-stage shrinkage, current/temperature, integration discrepancy, and at V360 extension scalars. Warp adds q/time at 3.90, 3.85, 3.80, 3.75, 3.70, 3.65, 3.60 V with already-passed masks and five-window phase/time summaries. A dimension-matched amplitude block adds mean, signed area, RMS, slope, and derivative extrema of registered residual voltage in five fixed-core windows. Match ridge penalties/effective degrees of freedom. It tests whether transparent landmarks/local vertical residuals suffice.

**Functional alternative.** Represent phase and amplitude separately by cubic B-splines with second-difference penalties or 1–4 training-only FPCA/PLS scores. Phase-only and amplitude-only branches get exactly K scores; combined gets K total scores split in safe inner folds. A 2K sensitivity gives the structured comparator 2K matched degrees of freedom. This alternative retains distributed correlated deformation lost by landmarks/windows; its value is resolving warp versus amplitude, not a small predictive gain.

A neural sequence model is deferred because safe family folds have only 5–8 independent specimens; revisit after reproducible low-rank underfit or 30 additional specimens per schedule. Mechanistic electrode fitting is deferred because tables lack independent half-cell anchors, rest/kinetic separation, and adjudicated mode truth.

## State reconstruction and forecast contrasts

Fit out-of-specimen, forward-date `G30`, `G44`, and `G360` reconstructions for `C[t]/C0` and, on resistance rows, `log(R[t]/R0)`. At each clock compare scalar-only, warp-only, amplitude-only, combined; report native MAE/RMSE, bias, calibration, family/stage influence, and reconstruction-error correlation with targets.

Freeze parent `H`, `Q30`, and `F30-T`. At q44/V360 fit:

- `D-G0`: history/q30 + generated current state + acquisition scalars, no post-q30 warp/amplitude;
- `D-GW`: D-G0 + structured/functional phase, rate, observation-length warp;
- `D-GWA`: D-GW + registered fixed-core amplitude;
- `D-T0`, `D-TW`, `D-TWA`: retrospective counterparts replacing generated by measured current state;
- `D-TWA-L`: amplitude affects only L;
- `D-TWA-S`: matched budget plus prespecified zero-sum horizon interaction for S and secondarily K;
- `Full-T`: completed-discharge upper comparator, not attribution evidence.

The decisive comparison is `D-TWA-S` versus `D-TW`: amplitude must improve slope after measured current capacity and all warp. `D-GWA` versus `D-GW` can reflect reconstruction correction. `D-TWA-S` versus `D-TWA-L` prevents level shifts being mislabeled trajectory.

With M family-balanced slope MAE, report at q44/V360:

- `I_wait=1-M(D-GWA)/M(F30-T)`;
- `I_warp=1-M(D-GW)/M(D-G0)`;
- `I_amp_gen=1-M(D-GWA)/M(D-GW)`;
- `I_amp_true=1-M(D-TWA-S)/M(D-TW)`;
- level-only amplitude and D-TWA-S versus D-TWA-L;
- matched V360 versus q44 extension value and fraction captured by extension scalars;
- reconstruction-error reduction and level-gain fraction captured by present state.

Use family-specific fits only where support permits; otherwise pooled hierarchical ridge with fixed family and training-only family-stage shrinkage. Use inherited earlier-family default penalties below 12 rows/two validation specimens. Never drop a family.

## Evaluation, controls, and uncertainty

Average loss over origins within specimen, specimens within family, then equally over five families. Jointly score three horizons on identical origins. Report capacity MAE/RMSE, L/S/K, native-unit errors, 90% training-only specimen-group conformal coverage/width, donor counts, and specimen/family/stage influence.

Use 10,000 paired trajectory bootstraps resampling whole specimens within family plus family-stage block bootstrap; the wider interval governs. Max-statistic simultaneous 95% intervals cover q44/V360, generated/measured state, structured/functional branches, three coordinates, and resistance. Families are fixed.

Controls:

1. dimension-matched sibling amplitude swap preserving warp;
2. sibling warp swap preserving amplitude;
3. held-specimen lagged amplitude/warp;
4. within-specimen time permutation;
5. target-trajectory/horizon shuffles;
6. current-state-label shuffle;
7. training-feature noise;
8. identity-warp, unregistered residual, tighter bounds;
9. x0/xG/xT and C/2 state sensitivities;
10. causal windows 1/101/501 and 3.75/3.45-V cutoffs;
11. no-family/no-stage diagnostic only;
12. correlations, VIF, and partial R2 of scores against duration, q increment, current, temperature, stage, family, C[t]/C0, and reconstruction error.

Target shuffling must remove gain. Swapped amplitude retaining advantage rejects specimen-specific amplitude attribution. Collinearity widens uncertainty; rows are not deleted to manufacture separation.

## Verdicts and falsification

Support **coordinate-robust registered-amplitude trajectory information** only if on both 200 and 166 sets:

1. V360 `I_wait`, `I_amp_gen`, and `I_amp_true` are each >=0.05 with simultaneous lower bounds >0;
2. D-TWA-S beats D-TW and D-TWA-L for S, not only L/vector average, with no horizon reversal;
3. q44 `I_amp_true` is positive with lower bound >0, proving fixed-support information;
4. structured/functional and x0/xG/xT signs agree; xT meets the 5% gate;
5. >=4 families improve, none worsens >5%, stage blocks retain sign, every leave-one-specimen aggregate is positive;
6. acquisition, coordinate, state, registration, cutoff, firewall, and controls pass.

Support a **capacity/time-warp or observation-length explanation** only if waiting or warp is useful (>=0.05, lower bound >0) while simultaneous upper bounds for q44 and V360 `I_amp_true` are <0.05 in both branches. If extension scalars capture >=80% of V360-over-q44 gain, call observation-length/acquisition proxy. If phase/rate retains value, call warp-associated prognosis. If generated-state amplitude improves but measured-state amplitude does not, call state-reconstruction correction. None is mechanism.

Call mixed if warp and measured-state amplitude pass. Gain only in L is level/state information, not trajectory. Resistance can corroborate with nominal/conservative agreement and two resistance definitions; it cannot rescue capacity.

Adverse amplitude evidence is upper bound <0.05 for `I_amp_true`; <=0 supports no benefit/possible harm. Adverse acquisition evidence is upper bound <0.05 for I_wait. If q30 matches q44/V360 while Full-T helps, information lies later. If state/warp match all curve models, amplitude is unnecessary at this resolution.

Inconclusive includes intervals crossing 0/0.05, q44/V360 or nominal/conservative conflict, coordinate/registration/branch reversal, family/specimen/stage dependence, inadequate coordinate overlap, unstable collinearity, poor state reconstruction/calibration, placebo retention, or endpoint disagreement. Preserve unfavorable results.

Invalid means source/join/clock failure, imputation, held-specimen/future leakage, preprocessing seeing validation specimens, post-clock sensitivity, row-random splitting, or systematic shuffled-target gain.

## Deliverable, compute, and adjudication boundary

Completion requires `source_audit.json`, `source_manifest.csv`, `boundary_order.parquet`, `forecast_origins.parquet`, `folds.csv`, `clock_events.parquet`, `feature_provenance.json`, `clock_firewalls.json`, `capacity_coordinates.parquet`, `expected_core_curves.parquet`, `registration_maps.parquet`, `phase_amplitude_features.parquet`, `state_crossfit_predictions.parquet`, `state_metrics.json`, `trajectory_targets.parquet`, `predictions.parquet`, `trajectory_metrics.json`, `attribution_contrasts.json`, `coordinate_sensitivity.json`, `negative_controls.json`, `uncertainty.parquet`, `influence.csv`, `model_artifacts/`, `environment.json`, `verdict.json`, and `report.md`. Every conclusion cites output fields.

Plan 12 CPUs, 64 GiB RAM, zero GPUs, 18,000 seconds, within 16 CPUs/262,144 MiB/28,800 seconds. The inherited boundary audit took 21.3 seconds; the new summary join took seconds. These establish input feasibility only. Elastic splines, low-rank FPCA/PLS, ridge, and grouped resampling are CPU-suitable. If runtime is tight, defer curvature, sparse resistance h=4, and 3.45-V sensitivity, never population, clocks, fixed-core decomposition, measured-state contrast, S, or falsification gates.

The simple model is retained because it tests interpretable sufficiency; the functional model is selected because distributed deformation is exactly what it loses. Neural/mechanistic alternatives are deferred for evidence reasons, not hardware labels.

A verifier can recompute hashes, members, schemas, joins, clocks, coordinates, templates, registration constraints, ancestry, folds, reconstructions, predictions, losses, intervals, controls, and verdict mapping. It must accept amplitude, warp-only, observation-length, state-correction, mixed, adverse, endpoint-specific, and inconclusive outcomes.

It cannot establish that registered amplitude is electrochemical state, identify LLI/LAM/plating/SEI, decide that measured current capacity is error-free/independent, prove interruption safety, or establish transfer beyond these schedules and Li/Kirkaldy lineage. Those require expert review, orthogonal/replicate state measurements, controlled current/rest perturbations, half-cell/post-mortem evidence, interrupted-versus-completed RPT experiments, and an independent cohort. Kirkaldy shares lineage and its experiment archives are unavailable; Severson is unavailable. Li et al. (2025) is used only through frozen review/configured files; unavailable full paper or supplementary methods were not inspected. This is adaptation, not reproduction.
